{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"body":"Research completion for lead-unpleasing-kitten (2026-08-16)\n\nDecision: do not implement broad cross-test scan-result reuse, fixture-scope promotion, node consolidation, cross-process caching, or xdist distribution changes without operator approval. Under `-n 3 --dist worksteal`, ordinary module/session fixtures are worker-local, so the measured reuse cannot be guaranteed without changing test structure or behavior. Safe first implementation is call-local OpenGrep validation deduplication keyed by detector `source_path` inside one `_run_opengrep` call; keep all scan invocations and unique external boundaries.\n\nEvidence:\n- Fresh origin/main `29448f61c095c4f63afb9291ae156a4e0163d843`; exact 31-node cohort passed in 82.23s on macOS/Python 3.12 with three worksteal workers.\n- Current >=1s call-phase sum 234.24 worker-seconds, down from puppylike-emo-rasbora's 250.81 at `80a69b0967`. Installed: Semgrep 1.172.0, ast-grep 0.45.1, gitleaks 8.30.1, scc 3.7.0, Universal Ctags 6.2.1; lizard absent.\n- Inventory: 2 Gitleaks config/secret nodes; 4 Python-oracle OpenGrep nodes; 2 OpenGrep timeout/invalid-detector conformance nodes; 3 public-exposure OpenGrep nodes; 5 mixed coverage nodes; 6 Engine-B Semgrep/ast-grep nodes; 4 conflict-marker OpenGrep nodes; 1 real Ctags corpus node; 2 grounding-info CLI/MCP schema nodes; 2 non-scan >=1s phases (Git-fixture setup and criterion-preview timeout). Exact node names and boundary mapping are in the ticket comment.\n- Matched AB/BA immutable-fixture experiments with exact output equality: five Python-oracle scans 28.727s -> 5.729s (22.998s); five mixed scans -> one standard plus one forced-metric-absence scan 40.668s -> 15.898s (24.770s); three identical JS scans 14.979s -> 5.039s (9.940s). Combined 84.373s -> 26.666s, saving 57.707s/68.4%. Mechanical projection is 234.24 -> 176.53 worker-seconds (24.6%), not wall time.\n- Conservative full-route claim is only 57.71 runner-seconds because CI does not pin analyzers and Ubuntu tool presence is unproven. Four-cell 230.83s is an upper bound, not an expected saving.\n- Call-local validation experiment: 11 detectors share five YAML sources. Two-call AB was 25.378s -> 13.692s; BA 26.671s -> 14.578s; median 26.025s -> 14.135s. Saving 11.890s/two calls or 5.945s/scan; validation subprocesses 22 -> 10; exact evidence equal.\n- Fault matrix retains discovery/loading, explicit tool absence/presence, process and real Semgrep timeouts, invalid-detector quarantine, path quarantine, standard plus forced-absence evidence accounting, and real advisory/blocking consumers. Direct exact-defect tests remain missing for malformed OpenGrep SARIF, ast-grep JSON, and metric JSON.\n- `test_ran_and_skipped_coexist_in_one_run` is misleading with scc present: unrelated skipped detectors satisfy the assertion, so it does not prove metric presence/absence.\n- OSS evidence: pip `e0a773b306c51debe77d21abf27ab86f06b379dd:tests/conftest.py`; pytest `604e2d0390c3850ded48788bdc9e4a5fb7013744:doc/en/how-to/fixtures.rst`; Semgrep `808ee51cda4f91d118fab80a411522e2cbbdc2fe:cli/tests/default/e2e/test_paths.py`. Interpretation: reuse immutable expensive setup, but retain bounded real CLI boundaries.\n- Tracker evidence: puppylike-emo-rasbora, shockproof-twill-porpoise, crushable-choosable-llama, rapid-cuboid-velvetcrab.\n- Created and linked bugs: `accepted-androgenic-elk` / `0024-fa99-d5bb-49bc` (scc invocation omits `--by-file`, so `Files: []` and metric detectors cannot emit file matches); `ferrety-crippling-dairycow` / `bdd8-8cfb-a752-4edc` (MCP grounding_info schema test emits unresolved lifespan forward-reference warning). Both remain open/unclaimed for rebar-debug.\n\nNo production/test files changed, no scanner invocation removed or mocked, and lead-unpleasing-kitten remains in progress pending the operator decision."},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"COMMENT","timestamp":1786911797383813001,"uuid":"badb2231-b6af-4b25-a8ea-de8d89d344d5"}